        "message": "Disable in-place goal rotation in the recovery profile\n\nProven deadlock from the October 23 GPU series trial 2: the goal checker\ntransforms the path end into the local costmap's odom frame at the\npath's planning stamp, so AMCL drift can hold that target outside\nxy tolerance while RPP's current-frame carrot is already inside. RPP's\nrotate-to-goal-heading then commands zero linear velocity and parks the\nrobot permanently between the two targets (measured: 0.185 m current vs\n0.203 m stale, 1.9 cm drift, five seconds of micro-rotation, checker\nnever firing). The passing trials won only by approach-creep momentum\nthrough the stale target - a coin flip on the drift. The straight 0.5 m\nprobe goal needs no in-place rotation; use_rotate_to_heading=false\nkeeps the approach creep carrying the robot to the checker's target,\nwith the 0.35 rad yaw tolerance covering the residual approach yaw.\nProfile change documented with the deadlock analysis; the checked-in\ncandidate YAML is regenerated and all 34 phase-5 + 170 safety tests\npass."
      },
      "type": "Git"
    },
